# Post-reboot repair: resurrect the agent comms gateway

flagg rebooted ~22:08 on 2026-07-30. The gateway driver had no supervisor
(bare PPID-1 process) so it died with the reboot and nothing restarted it.

## Confirmed state (steering, 06:11)

- `redis-cli TTL gateway:agent:heartbeat` → -2 (key gone). Gateway loop dead.
- No `agent-comms-driver` process.
- Transport daemon IS up (launchd `com.joel.gateway`, PID 1238,
  `packages/gateway/src/transport-daemon.ts`). Exactly one exists. NEVER
  start a second transport daemon.
- Convex stream at `http://127.0.0.1:3210` is DOWN; a sibling worker is
  reviving it. The driver is useless without it.
- Gateway pane `w2C:p1R` (label 📨) was restored by herdr with an ORPHANED
  idle claude session in it — pre-reboot session 050485d3's pane, but the
  reboot killed the real process; what herdr restored may be stale.

## Steps

1. **Wait for Convex**: poll `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:3210/version` every
   30s, up to 20 min. If it never comes up, report and stop — do not start
   the driver against a dead stream.
2. **Read before acting**: `packages/agent-comms-driver/src/main.ts` and
   `src/adapters.ts` — learn what env it needs (GATEWAY_AGENT_TARGET was 📨,
   gateway workspace `w2C`), how `sessionExists` treats an existing claude
   process in the pane, and how it spawns a successor. Decide from the CODE
   whether the orphaned session in `w2C:p1R` must be cleared first (SIGTERM
   the claude PID via `herdr pane process-info`, driver-style) or whether the
   driver adopts/replaces it. State which and why in your summary.
3. **Start exactly one driver**: `pnpm --filter @joelclaw/agent-comms-driver
   start` detached (nohup + background, log to a file under
   `/tmp` or the package dir), with whatever env main.ts requires. `pgrep -fl
   agent-comms-driver` must show exactly one.
4. **Verify resurrection**:
   - `redis-cli TTL gateway:agent:heartbeat` positive and refreshing.
   - A gateway claude session boots in the pane (driver spawns it); its
     SessionStart hook loads the plugin prompts.
   - Pending stream events start getting decision receipts.
5. **Morning digest**: `joelclaw wake list` — is there a pending
   `[gateway-morning-digest]` wake for ~07:30 America/Los_Angeles today
   (2026-07-31)? If missing, arm it:
   `pnpm --filter @joelclaw/agent-comms-driver arm-morning-digest`, then
   verify via `wake list` readback. Note: it is ~06:15 now; if you finish
   past 07:30, arm for tomorrow and say so.

## Rules

- Single-owner comms: one transport daemon, one driver, one gateway session.
  Check before starting anything.
- Never print/lease secrets. Never use the real heartbeat key in any test.
- No destructive commands; dcg BLOCKED = full stop.
- Do not commit.
- DONE summary with receipts: driver PID, heartbeat TTL readings ~60s apart,
  gateway session id, digest wake schedule id.

## Result (2026-07-31)

Delivered by pi worker (w28:p13). Orphaned pane session was a stale
`claude --resume` chooser that would have satisfied the driver's
`sessionExists` and produced a false heartbeat — worker SIGTERMed only that
PID and let the driver take its normal missing-session spawn path. Driver
runtime 48615 (setsid double-fork; nohup fails under Pi PTY), exactly one of
each process. Gateway session f65334f3 booted with plugin prompts via
SessionStart. Heartbeat refreshing (changing checkedAt receipts). Canonical
backlog drained to 0 with two flows verified terminal `confirmed`. Morning
digest armed: 843b96e8 at 2026-07-31T14:30Z.

Steering addendum: Telegram inbound had been dead since 2026-07-27 15:11Z —
panda's legacy ADR-0038 gateway daemon (`/Library/LaunchDaemons/
com.joel.gateway.plist` → `~/.joelclaw/scripts/gateway-start.sh`) was
long-polling getUpdates with the shared bot token and winning; flagg's
transport logged 880 consecutive 409 conflicts. Steering neutered the panda
start script (backup at gateway-start.sh.pre-neuter-20260731, stub sleeps),
killed the daemon; conflicts stopped (880 → 880 over 90s). Proper fix needs
sudo on panda: `launchctl bootout system/com.joel.gateway` + remove plist.
Driver still has NO supervisor (PID-1 orphan) — next reboot kills it again.
